{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1383007-looking-for-feedback-on-chrod-webtools","id":1383007,"title":"Looking for feedback on ChroD webtools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-21T11:22:09-07:00","id":1383007,"title":"Looking for feedback on ChroD webtools","content":"Hey guys, not a regular poster, but I have something you might find interesting. It's a web-based character sheet thrown together in a couple days. It's rough but working and I'm looking for feedback and gauging interest. It's nearly good enough for my personal use, but if there's something that sucks about it for your use-case let me know.<br /> <br /> If anyone out there is like me, dealing with PDF readers, crashes, forgetting where you saved files, and long load up times and domineering windows can sometimes drive you to the brink of insanity. I just want a light weight URL that I can bookmark, pull up instantly, reads great on half a screen, and looks clean.<br /> <br /> Being that it's very early here are the things that I already plan to add:<br /> \u25cf More themes<br /> \u25cf Character sharing with hashed urls (requires a database and this won't be it's permanent home if I work on this more)<br /> <br /> And some known issues that are easy to fix I'm just tired after a day and a half of work:<br /> \u25cf Saving and loading characters from file aren't implemented<br /> \u25cf Looks pretty bad on 4K or small phones<br /> <br /> EDIT: Lastest version of the sheet editor is here now<br /> <a href=\"http://cofdsheet.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cofdsheet.com/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","user":"CoraBlue","date":". 04-26-2020, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","name":"CoraBlue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T11:49:55-07:00","id":1383011,"title":"","content":"Initial observations:<ul><li>The lack of a space for themed characters' Disciplines, Arcana, Contracts, etc. is a definite drawback. That's page 1 material. There'd be room for it by cutting down on Conditions and Aspirations space; non-mages definitely don't need 7 lines to write down their 3 aspirations.</li> <li>Themes could be improved by changing the Virtue, Vice, Calling, and Faction lines at the top to their respective terms; I assume this is already on the to-do list.</li> <li>The Changeling theme requires ticks in addition to dots for Clarity.</li> <li>&quot;Investigate&quot; and &quot;Animal&quot; should be &quot;Investigation&quot; and &quot;Animal Ken&quot; ideally.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T00:26:10-07:00","id":1383108,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your feedback! I mainly play Mortal, so when this started during the initial layout I used that as a base and sort of spaced on splat abilities. I'll definitely put those in. As for the skill names I'll take this under advisement for sure. It's a balance between readability at smaller window scales and faithfulness and both have their pros and cons. I'll also have to brush up on my Changeling.<br /> <br /> Really appreciate you taking the time to check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","name":"CoraBlue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T08:15:26-07:00","id":1383142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1383007-looking-for-feedback-on-chrod-webtools?p=1383011#post1383011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of a space for themed characters' Disciplines, Arcana, Contracts, etc. is a definite drawback. That's page 1 material. There'd be room for it by cutting down on Conditions and Aspirations space; non-mages definitely don't need 7 lines to write down their 3 aspirations.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 is probably a good middle ground for Aspiration space, given that two separate axes of Werewolf give characters an extra Aspiration, Arisen or cultists thereof can have a Condition that gives them two extra Aspirations as long as it lasts, Sin-Eaters start with an extra one that's part of their core template, vampire colonies are built with a shared Aspiration, and there's a core Merit in Promethean that includes declaring an extra Aspiration, on top of non-Tremere Mage characters below Gnosis 6 only having one or two Obsessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Forgot about Memory Bleed. 04-24-2020, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T01:33:49-07:00","id":1383531,"title":"","content":"Updated the sheet. ctrl+F5 if you have it cached so it loads properly.<br /> <br /> I went ahead and took most of the suggestions here and rearranged some things to make sure page 1 still looks really nice even at half width. Because of the reformat saves got borked but I don't expect anyone is actually using this yet anyway. Health ticks also save properly now.<br /> <br /> Once I add a page 2, which should just be another couple hours of work once I have time, I'll try and find a permanent home for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","name":"CoraBlue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T17:26:23-07:00","id":1384061,"title":"","content":"Updated the sheet again. Would really appreciate some additional feedback. Now at a dedicated URL.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://cofdsheet.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cofdsheet.com/</a><br /> <br /> I plan to implement the sidebar in a completely different way so it's always accessible. Vampire theme is also unfinished. I also plan to implement a database so sheets can be shared. Work on this is slower than I'd like but my free time is currently pretty limited.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","name":"CoraBlue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T14:56:37-07:00","id":1385662,"title":"","content":"Hey nice project. I would encourage to give it desktop to mobile responsiveness so similar to bootstrap col-md-4 and col-sm-12 where it automatically responds and reflow for smaller screens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T19:20:37-07:00","id":1385714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoraBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1383007-looking-for-feedback-on-chrod-webtools?p=1384061#post1384061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updated the sheet again. Would really appreciate some additional feedback. Now at a dedicated URL.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://cofdsheet.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cofdsheet.com/</a><br /> <br /> I plan to implement the sidebar in a completely different way so it's always accessible. Vampire theme is also unfinished. I also plan to implement a database so sheets can be shared. Work on this is slower than I'd like but my free time is currently pretty limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any way to have it auto-fill calculated values (e.g. Willpower, Health)? Or at least list their default values so that you don't have to look them up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T22:23:28-07:00","id":1390198,"title":"","content":"I would expand the XP section<br /> <br /> Total XP<br /> Spent XP<br /> Remaining XP ( calcs Total less Spent)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T14:17:25-07:00","id":1390378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoraBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1383007-looking-for-feedback-on-chrod-webtools?p=1384061#post1384061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updated the sheet again. Would really appreciate some additional feedback. Now at a dedicated URL.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://cofdsheet.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cofdsheet.com/</a><br /> <br /> I plan to implement the sidebar in a completely different way so it's always accessible. Vampire theme is also unfinished. I also plan to implement a database so sheets can be shared. Work on this is slower than I'd like but my free time is currently pretty limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>The decision to add Extended Attributes but not Extended Skills is an odd one; both can be raised above 5 in typically the same situations.<br /> If Notes is intended as a space for answering the breaking point questions, a separate space for listing breaking points is probably not necessary.<br /> The Vampire template doesn't need a section for breaking points; detachment risks don't vary from vampire to vampire. It does need a section for Touchstones.<br /> The Mage template also doesn't need a section for breaking points. Optionally it could use a separate header for Obsessions, but this is not as big a deal, as they can be listed pretty comfortably under Aspirations. The Rotes and Praxes section could probably be better replaced by a line or checkboxes for each Spell to indicate which are praxes or rotes.<br /> The Changeling template probably doesn't need such a large section for Goblin Debt. It's a single-digit number. Like 5. 5 Goblin Debt.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the Blessings &amp; Curses section in the Changeling template is for, or the Potency column on page 2 for powers if it is distinct from Damage, Effect, <i>and</i> Dice Pool. The Damage column can probably be removed, listing any power damage under Effect instead; direct damage powers don't make up a large enough proportion of powers in general to eat up a column.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}